# Title: Bad Opsec Defaults Sacrificial Processes With Improper Arguments
# ID: a7c3d773-caef-227e-a7e7-c2f13c622329
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Oleg Kolesnikov @securonix invrep_de, oscd.community, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2020-10-23
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.011
# Description: Detects attackers using tooling with bad opsec defaults.
# E.g. spawning a sacrificial process to inject a capability into the process without taking into account how the process is normally run.
# One trivial example of this is using rundll32.exe without arguments as a sacrificial process (default in CS, now highlighted by c2lint), running WerFault without arguments (Kraken - credit am0nsec), and other examples.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_path="*\\regasm.exe" AND process_exec="*regasm.exe") OR (process_path="*\\regsvcs.exe" AND process_exec="*regsvcs.exe") OR (process_path="*\\regsvr32.exe" AND process_exec="*regsvr32.exe") OR (process_path="*\\rundll32.exe" AND process_exec="*rundll32.exe") OR (process_path="*\\WerFault.exe" AND process_exec="*WerFault.exe")) AND NOT ((((parent_process_path="*\\AppData\\Local\\BraveSoftware\\Brave-Browser\\Application\\*" OR parent_process_path="*\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\*") AND parent_process_path="*\\Installer\\setup.exe" AND parent_process_exec="*--uninstall *" AND process_path="*\\rundll32.exe" AND process_exec="*rundll32.exe") OR (parent_process_path="*\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\EdgeUpdate\\Install\\{*" AND process_path="*\\rundll32.exe" AND process_exec="*rundll32.exe"))))
